{
  "Comment": [
    "ExyokiOffice-owned overlay on the imported schema metadata under data/schemas.",
    "Several element classes can declare one qualified element name - w:rPr is the run properties of a",
    "paragraph mark and the run properties of a style, x:sheetData is a worksheet's cell table and an",
    "Office2010 extension - so the element factory, which resolves a name without knowing the parent, has",
    "to be told which class a bare name creates. Parsing that walks the parent's content model keeps",
    "resolving the name through the particle tree and is unaffected. Without this file the winner would be",
    "whatever an unstable sort left in front, which differs between standard library implementations and",
    "made the same package parse into different classes on Windows and Linux. Keys are namespace URIs and",
    "local names from data/schemas; a name the schemas no longer declare ambiguously fails the build, and",
    "an ambiguous name missing here is reported as a generator warning."
  ],
